<h1>Welcome!</h1>

<p>Hello and welcome to my corner of the internet. I'm Amey Ambade, a Lead Data Scientist with a curiosity that extends far beyond the world of data.</p>

<p>I built this site to be a home for my thoughts, explorations, and adventures. Here's what you can expect to find:</p>

<h2>What I'll Write About</h2>

<h3>Technical Deep Dives</h3>

<p>Data science is my profession, and I love diving deep into complex problems. I'll share tutorials, code walkthroughs, and lessons learned from real-world projects. Expect topics like machine learning, statistical analysis, data engineering, and the tools I use daily.</p>

<h3>Industry Opinions</h3>

<p>The field of data science and AI is evolving rapidly. I have thoughts about where we're heading, what practices we should adopt (and abandon), and how to navigate this changing landscape. These posts will be more opinionated and hopefully spark some interesting discussions.</p>

<h3>Hobby Explorations</h3>

<p>Life is too short to only do one thing. I maintain a bucket list of hobbies I want to try, and when I check one off, I'll write about the experience. Whether it's learning to play piano, trying pottery, or running a half marathon, these posts will document my journey as a perpetual beginner.</p>

<h2>Why a Personal Site?</h2>

<p>In an age of social media feeds and algorithmic timelines, there's something refreshing about having your own space on the web. This site is:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Intentional:</strong> Every piece of content here is something I chose to create and share.</li>
  <li><strong>Permanent:</strong> Unlike social posts that disappear into the void, these writings have a home.</li>
  <li><strong>Personal:</strong> This is me, unfiltered by platform constraints or engagement algorithms.</li>
</ul>

<h2>A Note of Inspiration</h2>

<p>The design and approach of this site was inspired by <a href="https://rafa.design" target="_blank">Rafael Conde's portfolio</a>. I loved how his site balanced professional work with personal touches, and I've tried to capture that same spirit while making it my own.</p>

<h2>What's Next?</h2>

<p>I'm still setting things up, but expect more content soon. In the meantime, feel free to explore the site, check out my hobbies bucket list, or find me on the various social platforms linked below.</p>

<p>Thanks for stopping by!</p>

<p><em>— Amey</em></p>
